      "role": "user",
      "content": "Interesting. You mentioned Snippet B has \"grammatical errors.\" If we were to look past the syntax and just focus on the actual content—the message is exactly the same as Snippet A. They are both communicating a strategic pivot based on quarterly data. \n\nWhy does the specific way the information is phrased in B make it significantly less professional? Is it just the dialect, or does the way it's written suggest a lower level of competence or education for the speaker compared to someone using the phrasing in A?",
