      "content": "The reduced professionalism in Snippet B stems from several factors beyond just dialect, primarily concerning register and diction. The contractions, use of phrasal verbs (\"change up,\" \"keep the money comin' in\"), and informal grammar directly signal a lower register of communication. In a C-suite context, this phrasing can subtly imply a lack of polish, precise analytical skill, or formal education, which undermines confidence in the message itself. Essentially, the mechanics of the language are interpreted as a reflection of the speaker's business formality.",
