      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, that is precisely the association the language carries in many professional contexts; linguistic features are often subconsciously linked to perceived competence. Certain grammatical deviations and colloquialisms are culturally codified markers of non-standardized language varieties. In the professional sphere, the adherence to Standard English is treated as a required performance of competence and education. Therefore, deviations from this accepted standard can unfortunately lead to immediate, rapid attributions of lower analytical skill rather than the objective evaluation of the underlying idea.",
